{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105552",
      "title": "Array & Object Types",
      "lectureOrder": 753,
      "videoOrder": 693,
      "sourceHash": "f32dda55a2b30c8fb9dc0f2bbc4c99a84a18ec6090df7638226f697a74f2f2f1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.02,
          "end": 5.74,
          "en": "Now let's talk about the more complex types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.74,
          "end": 8.62,
          "en": "So arrays and objects here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.62,
          "end": 10.96,
          "en": "And let's start with arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.96,
          "end": 15.89,
          "en": "If I have my hobbies, that might be an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.89,
          "end": 18.71,
          "en": "Hence this type assignment is wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.71,
          "end": 22,
          "en": "This allows me to store a single string and hobbies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22,
          "end": 24.263,
          "en": "but I want to have an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 28.66,
          "en": "To tell Typescript that I want an array of strings in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.66,
          "end": 32.29,
          "en": "we can instead assign this type string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.29,
          "end": 35.01,
          "en": "with square brackets thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.01,
          "end": 36.73,
          "en": "This tells TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.73,
          "end": 40.8,
          "en": "that we want to have an array of strings in hobbies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.8,
          "end": 44.18,
          "en": "And of course we could have to same with an array of numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.18,
          "end": 46.59,
          "en": "and array of Booleans, whatever.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.59,
          "end": 48.62,
          "en": "But here I want to have an array of strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.62,
          "end": 51.35,
          "en": "and that allows me to store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.35,
          "end": 54.34,
          "en": "an array of strings in there, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.34,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "Now this is possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 60.32,
          "en": "If I would add a number, in addition to the strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.32,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "I again would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 63.57,
          "en": "because that's not a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.57,
          "end": 65.35,
          "en": "and I'm making it very clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.35,
          "end": 69.82,
          "en": "that only an array of strings may be stored in hobbies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.82,
          "end": 72.98,
          "en": "So that's how we can set up array types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.98,
          "end": 76.72,
          "en": "Now we also can set types for entire objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.72,
          "end": 78.97,
          "en": "Let's say I have a person variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.97,
          "end": 82.57,
          "en": "and in there I don't wanna store a name or an age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.57,
          "end": 84.08,
          "en": "but an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.08,
          "end": 88.01,
          "en": "I want to be able to store something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.01,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "An object with a name and an age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 93.35300000000001,
          "en": "Something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.35300000000001,
          "end": 95.163,
          "en": "That should be stored in person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 98.7,
          "en": "Now, of course, this works like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.7,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "because TypeScript out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 104.65,
          "en": "without configuration is quite forgiving.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.65,
          "end": 108.47,
          "en": "And it by default allows me to store any value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.47,
          "end": 109.66,
          "en": "in a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.66,
          "end": 112.95,
          "en": "It has a special any type for this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 115.22,
          "en": "which we can see if we have our person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.22,
          "end": 118.75999999999999,
          "en": "The default type assumed is the any type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.75999999999999,
          "end": 121.76,
          "en": "which we can all say explicitly set like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.76,
          "end": 123.97,
          "en": "Which simply tells TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.97,
          "end": 125.5,
          "en": "I don't wanna tell you anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.5,
          "end": 128.78,
          "en": "about the types of values stored in this variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.78,
          "end": 130.79,
          "en": "Anything is allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.79,
          "end": 134.35,
          "en": "And that of course is a fallback type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.35,
          "end": 136.54,
          "en": "which you typically should not use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.54,
          "end": 139.34,
          "en": "because that kind of defeats the entire purpose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.34,
          "end": 141.84,
          "en": "of using TypeScript in the first place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 143.25,
          "en": "With the any type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 147.16,
          "en": "you are basically back to standard Javascript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.16,
          "end": 148.18,
          "en": "So it's the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.18,
          "end": 151.15,
          "en": "but of course it's not what I wanna keep here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.15,
          "end": 153.67000000000002,
          "en": "Instead I wanna make it very clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.67000000000002,
          "end": 157.45,
          "en": "which kind of object can be stored in person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.45,
          "end": 160.34,
          "en": "I wanna allow this object for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.34,
          "end": 163.69,
          "en": "but storing another object with a different structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.69,
          "end": 167.17000000000002,
          "en": "Where I have let's say just a Boolean in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.17000000000002,
          "end": 169.93,
          "en": "That's something I don't wanna allow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 169.93,
          "end": 172.78,
          "en": "And for this, we can again add a type assignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 172.78,
          "end": 176.01,
          "en": "but now we wanna add an object type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.01,
          "end": 178.81,
          "en": "A type defining an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.81,
          "end": 181.73,
          "en": "And for this, we then add curly-braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.73,
          "end": 184.63,
          "en": "just as we do it when we create an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.63,
          "end": 186.87,
          "en": "But please note that this is not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.87,
          "end": 189.3,
          "en": "on the right side of an equal sign here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 189.3,
          "end": 191.79,
          "en": "So we're not creating our object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.79,
          "end": 195.42,
          "en": "Instead here, it's in the place where we set a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 195.42,
          "end": 198.26,
          "en": "for a variable on the right side of this colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 198.26,
          "end": 200.313,
          "en": "after the variable name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 200.313,
          "end": 202.99,
          "en": "And thefore this here is actually a type assignment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.99,
          "end": 205.38,
          "en": "And hence here, we're not creating an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 205.38,
          "end": 208.45,
          "en": "but instead we're using a TypeScript feature here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 208.45,
          "end": 211.76,
          "en": "which is the object type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 211.76,
          "end": 214.52,
          "en": "So we're defining the type for an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 214.52,
          "end": 217.62,
          "en": "We're defining the structure of an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 217.62,
          "end": 221.21,
          "en": "And here we can then for example, say that person",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 221.21,
          "end": 224.28,
          "en": "should store objects that have a name field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 224.28,
          "end": 228.02,
          "en": "where the value of that name field is a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.02,
          "end": 231.93,
          "en": "and which have a age field where the value is number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.93,
          "end": 235.81,
          "en": "So where the value is of type number, I should say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 235.81,
          "end": 240.15,
          "en": "And with that, we're telling TypeScript that only objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.15,
          "end": 243.46,
          "en": "that have this kind of type should be storable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 243.46,
          "end": 245.51,
          "en": "in that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.51,
          "end": 248.54,
          "en": "That's why I can store this object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.54,
          "end": 252.36,
          "en": "because that object down there has exactly the structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.36,
          "end": 253.9,
          "en": "I'm defining here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 253.9,
          "end": 256.94,
          "en": "It has a name field, which has a string as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 256.94,
          "end": 260.64,
          "en": "and a age field, which has a number as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.64,
          "end": 261.79,
          "en": "On the otherhand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 261.79,
          "end": 265.25,
          "en": "this object down here is not storable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 265.25,
          "end": 267.12,
          "en": "And hence, I'm getting an error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 267.12,
          "end": 269.95,
          "en": "because it is having the wrong type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.95,
          "end": 272.21,
          "en": "This objects type would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 272.21,
          "end": 274.92,
          "en": "that it has an isEmployee field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 274.92,
          "end": 277.56,
          "en": "which stores a value of type Boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 277.56,
          "end": 281.49,
          "en": "Which does not match this type description here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 281.49,
          "end": 283.52,
          "en": "So, comment this out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 283.52,
          "end": 287.593,
          "en": "And that's how we can define array types and object types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.6,
          "end": 291.13,
          "en": "Of course, we could also combine these two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 291.13,
          "end": 294.43,
          "en": "If I wanted to have an array full of people.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 294.43,
          "end": 299.18,
          "en": "So full off people that have this type signature here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 299.18,
          "end": 303.27,
          "en": "then I could set the type of people here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 303.27,
          "end": 305.42,
          "en": "to this object type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 305.42,
          "end": 306.91,
          "en": "So I'm repeating this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 306.91,
          "end": 311.38,
          "en": "but as an array by adding square brackets thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 311.38,
          "end": 314.29,
          "en": "Now I'm saying in people,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 314.29,
          "end": 317.93,
          "en": "I don't wanna store a single object of that structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 317.93,
          "end": 321.103,
          "en": "but an array of such objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 322.05,
          "end": 325.55,
          "en": "And that's how we can then already get a bit more advanced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 325.55,
          "end": 328.83,
          "en": "by combining different TypeScript features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 328.83,
          "end": 331.723,
          "en": "and by combining different types.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
